    <!-- Guided tour and about -->
    <string name="tour_title_scope_business">Business and Units</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_scope_business">Select and manage your business ventures and active branches or outlets. Each venture\'s data is fully isolated — transactions, reports, and backups are all independent. Removing one venture does not affect any other.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_scope_book">Plan vs Actual Ledgers</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_scope_book">Plan (budget/RAB) and Actual (cash on hand) books are strictly separated. Fill in the Plan before launching as a cost simulation, record Actual during operations, then compare both in Reports → Comparison tab to judge your planning accuracy.</string>
    <string name="tour_title_hero_summary">Financial Executive Summary</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_hero_summary">See your cash balance, net profit, and money in and out at a glance. If the balance looks negative while you still have money on hand, the opening capital is probably missing: record it as Money in under \"Setoran Modal Pemilik\" (owner capital).</string>
    <string name="tour_title_cost_chart">Cost breakdown</string>
    <string name="tour_desc_cost_chart">Every expense is sorted automatically into expense categories tailored to your industry (inventory stock, ingredients, wages, rent, packaging, or operations). Watch your highest spending areas to protect profit margins.</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_kinds_title">Choose the kind of transaction</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_kinds_desc">Choose Money in or Money out, then a category. The category decides the kind of record: owner capital is not counted as income, and owner drawings and equipment purchases are not counted as expenses. Add volume and unit if you want the unit price calculated.</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_history_title">Transaction history</string>
    <string name="tour_entry_history_desc">Everything you have recorded lives in the History tab on the bottom bar, with search and filters for money in, money out, and unpaid.</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_tabs_title">Three points of view</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_tabs_desc">Profit, Loss and Cash Flow answers \"what did I make\", Feasibility and Capital answers \"is this worth continuing\", and Actual vs Target answers \"how far did actual drift from plan\".</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_profit_title">Profit and cash flow</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_profit_desc">Net profit = operating income − operating cost. Because every record is cash, profit equals operating cash flow. Owner capital, drawings and equipment purchases never change profit; they show under financing or investing cash flow.</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_feasibility_title">BEP, Unit Cost (HPP), and Profit Margins</string>
    <string name="tour_reports_feasibility_desc">Break-even rupiah: the minimum revenue that avoids a loss. Break-even volume: the minimum units/servings that covers every cost. Unit Cost (HPP): what one unit costs you to produce or buy — selling above it yields gross profit. B/C ratio: revenue divided by cost; above 1 the business is viable. Fill in the assumptions under Edit Assumptions to make these indicators appear.</string>
